ndidate; single-b matches. Seed IDs, fingerprint and compiled-pair-draft status remain unchanged; no bespoke pairs or supporting seeds were supplied.","compatible":true}]},"preserveFirstPass":true,"frozenExampleIds":["S41-single-a","S41-single-b","S42-single-a","S42-single-b","S43-single-a","S43-single-b","S44-single-a","S44-single-b","S45-single-a","S45-single-b","S46-single-a","S46-single-b","S47-single-b","S48-single-a","S48-single-b","S49-single-a","S49-single-b","S50-single-a","S50-single-b"],"instruction":"Reuse the saved writer artifact. Preserve every firstPass rating and evidence exactly. Copy frozen records unchanged. Correct only rejected candidate dialogues and their decision/rationale/reservation as necessary. Do not regenerate the whole batch. Return the complete artifact with unchanged records copied exactly.","writerBindingReservations":[{"key":"S43","assessment":"The transfer itself remains semantically compatible: its action restores placement and sequence, opening prioritizes the usual step, response predicts unraveling, challenge proposes another way, and closing seeks reassurance through completion. Revised a preserves tea-shoes-keys and threatened repacking; revised b preserves curtains before cat feeding and makes breakfast depend on restoring the sequence. Both stored seedBindingHashes identify original text and require integration-side rebinding. The D32 instruction requires someone else to test a shortcut, substitute or questionable fix before A relies on it; its repaired-tap and coffee-substitute seeds support delegated testing. However, the saved writer reservation remains unresolved: both bespoke seedUse fields say A 'permits a shortcut only as someone else's contained trial,' while S43+D32-a A1 requires the order to remain exactly intact and B2 makes tea take longer. S43+D32-b A1/A3 supports a trial outside the routine, but cannot repair a's description. Safe unchanged rebinding of the full bespoke provenance therefore remains unestablished. Preserve both pair dialogues, seedRefs, exact seedUse fields, reviewedCardFingerprints, version 0.25.0, internal-editorial-pass statuses, all four supporting-seed sourceHashes and original supporting dialogues. Preserve transfer cardId, fingerprint, seedIds and compiled-pair-draft status. This pending binding assessment does not rescore either pair.","compatible":false}]}
